Z||000000||Kage86GT4SP||06-20-99||11:31 AM||||Well, I climbed around my new family member, and discovered the ebrake cable to the passenger side was rusted solid, naturally in the "on" position.<p>I ordered another one from the neighborhood parts house ($15.00 or so - and picking up yet another Haynes manual!) which will be here Monday.<p>I have kept your responses and added them to my Fiero File.  Man, am I glad I found this site!<p>K.
Z||000001||lowCG||06-20-99||01:59 PM||||Hey! You lucked out ,more less.<br>I'd check the pads out to make sure they didn't get heat damaged,they can de-laminate from this kind of thing(lifting,noticeable on the edges)or begin to dissintegrate/crack.<br>Just having been glazed over can reduce the stopping ability,but a quick hit on a sander will fix if that's all that happened.
Z||000002||batboy||06-20-99||02:56 PM||||Sanding the glaze off of brake pads and shoes is a big no-no. Although all of us shade tree mechanics have done it from time to time, including me (shame, shame). Older brake linings often had asbestos in them. Warning: DO NOT breathe the dust. Wear a face mask or put a bandana over your mouth and nose like the old western bandits. Better yet, especially if loved ones such as kids and/or significant others might be driving it, just spring for a new set of pads. They don't cost that much and are cheap insurance, in my humble opinion.
Z||000003||lowCG||06-20-99||03:39 PM||||We've conducted an inspection(sattelite imaging)of your exhaust emissions and found a high amount of hydrocarbon/NO2 coming from the rear of your fiero BATBOY! <br>So I'd be wanting to give all the kids,animals,bugs,and other organisms a fighting chance and go out,right away,and buy 4 catalysts for that rocket-car of yours!<br>But really,I wouldn't want to breath that stuff either,and would recommend new pads of a reputable brand,like Raybestos delux grade,or Autospecialty,and not just the ones they hand you for $10 a set.
Z||000004||batboy||06-20-99||07:20 PM||||Uh oh, busted! Yes, I know, I'm beginning to sound like my father with all the cautions. Also, I'm guilty of running my vehicles without Cat-licking Converters. Out here on the prairie, we are lucky not to have any type of vehicle inspections. Mainly because hardly anyone lives out here. I'm goin' to fetch me up my huntin' rifle right now and shoot down that pesky satellite, so y'all can't spy on me no more.
Z||000005||theogre||06-21-99||12:03 AM||||Don't forget to run the VIN past the Pontiac help desk. (1800PMCARES) That will tell you what is any recalls are outstanding. There are 1 or 2 for the brakes.
